frame(v = [NA, 3, NA]).add(f = fill_missing(v, 0, method: forward))
---
error[Z0410]: `fill_missing` takes a value or `method:`, not both
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:59
  |
1 | frame(v = [NA, 3, NA]).add(f = fill_missing(v, 0, method: forward))
  |                                                           ^^^^^^^ given beside a value
  |
  = help: `fill_missing(x, 0)` puts 0 where `x` is NA; `fill_missing(x, method: forward)` carries the last value down

frame(v = [NA, 3, NA]).add(f = fill_missing(v))
---
error[Z0406]: `fill_missing` needs a value or `method:`
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:32
  |
1 | frame(v = [NA, 3, NA]).add(f = fill_missing(v))
  |                                ^^^^^^^^^^^^ neither is given
  |
  = help: usage: `fill_missing(x, 0)` to fill with a value, or `fill_missing(x, method: forward)` to carry the last value down

let d = frame(v = [NA, 3, NA])
fill_missing(d["v"], method: forward)
---
error[Z0602]: `fill_missing` with `method:` follows the rows of a frame and stands inside `add` or `update`
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:1
  |
2 | fill_missing(d["v"], method: forward)
  | ^^^^^^^^^^^^ no frame here
  |
  = help: write it inside a definition, as in `wages.add(filled = fill_missing(wage, method: forward))`

fill_missing(3, method: backward)
